ll moving away from the target and remaining > 35. Keep the first-step rule (empty memory: choose A, no point) and keep 'never choose A after the first step'. Keep the fallback: if crossings exceeds N-1, choose C if the cube is heading toward the target or stopped, otherwise B. Note that the policy must update memory (crossings, cube_side, first_cross_t) before applying these rules, since the crossing that makes crossings reach N-1 often happens inside the frames of the very step where the decision is made."}

